51
00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:15.990 line:8% position:50% align:center size:90%
Look at my pride! She wanted to ask
for forgiveness, but I wouldn’t give in.

52
00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:21.430 line:8% position:50% align:center size:90%
Humility. It was self-examination,
looking within myself,

53
00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:25.470 line:8% position:50% align:center size:90%
and it brought reactions.
Those changes reached my wife, too.

54
00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:30.050 line:8% position:50% align:center size:90%
On a conjugal visit: “You’re different—
your behavior, your attitude.”

55
00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:33.770 line:8% position:50% align:center size:90%
Even my own family has noticed
a big difference in me, you know?

56
00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:37.350 line:8% position:50% align:center size:90%
More at ease, calmer,
really much more at ease.

57
00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:43.590 line:8% position:50% align:center size:90%
A letter using individuation, a virtue,
brought my daughter to visit me.

58
00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:48.250 line:8% position:50% align:center size:90%
I was the kind of man who couldn’t
go to my son and tell him

59
00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:49.970 line:8% position:50% align:center size:90%
